[{"category":"section","location":"api/#API-Reference","page":"API Reference","text":"The API reference below is generated from docstrings in the source code.","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Index","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Index"},{"category":"section","location":"api/#Docstrings","page":"API Reference","text":"","title":"Docstrings"},{"category":"method","location":"api/#AllInOne.hello-Tuple{}","page":"API Reference","text":"hello() -> String\n\n\nReturn a friendly greeting.\n\nExamples\n\njulia> AllInOne.hello()\n\"Hello, World!\"\n\n\n\n\n\n","title":"AllInOne.hello"},{"category":"section","location":"user/#User-Guide","page":"User Guide","text":"Before starting the tutorial, complete the Quick Start section. Feature requests and bug reports are handled through GitHub Issues.","title":"User Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"user/#Tutorial","page":"User Guide","text":"julia> import AllInOne\njulia> AllInOne.hello()\n\"Hello, World!\"","title":"Tutorial"},{"category":"section","location":"user/#Examples","page":"User Guide","text":"import AllInOne\ntext_1 = AllInOne.hello()\ntext_2 = \"Goodbye, World!\"\ntext_1 * \" \" * text_2\n\"Hello, World! Goodbye, World!\"","title":"Examples"},{"category":"section","location":"developer/#developer-guide","page":"Developer Guide","text":"If you are planning significant changes, open an issue first. The ColPrac guidelines are recommended. For Julia package development basics, see:\n\nHow to develop a Julia package\nPkg: Creating packages","title":"Developer Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"developer/#local-setup","page":"Developer Guide","text":"This procedure is required only once. Install Git and Julia on your local machine before starting.\n\nFork the repository on GitHub.\nClone the forked repository. Replace xxxxxx with your GitHub username.\ngit clone https://github.com/xxxxxx/AllInOne.jl.git\ncd AllInOne.jl\nInstall development tools: Revise.jl and Runic.jl.\njulia --startup-file=no -e 'import Pkg; Pkg.add(\"Revise\")'\njulia --project=@runic --startup-file=no -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.add(\"Runic\")'","title":"One-Time Local Setup"},{"category":"section","location":"developer/#development-flow","page":"Developer Guide","text":"This is the typical workflow for making changes.\n\nCreate a branch for your changes. Replace xxx with the issue number (e.g. issue/123).\ncd AllInOne.jl\ngit switch -c issue/xxx\nStart an interactive session with Revise.jl.\njulia --startup-file=no -i -e 'using Revise; import Pkg; Pkg.activate(\".\"); using AllInOne'\nChange the source code:\nWhen making new functions or updating docstrings, refer to Documenter: Adding docstrings.\nIf you need a new dependency, use julia --project=. --startup-file=no -e 'import Pkg; Pkg.add(\"SomePackage\"); Pkg.resolve(); Pkg.instantiate()'. Replace SomePackage with the actual package name.\nFormat the source code with Runic.jl.\njulia --project=@runic --startup-file=no -e 'using Runic; exit(Runic.main(ARGS))' -- --inplace .\nRun the tests. It will take a few minutes.\njulia --project=. --startup-file=no -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.test()'\nBuild the documentation locally. HTML files (docs/build/*.html) will be generated. Check them with Chrome or any other web browsers.\njulia --project=docs --startup-file=no -e 'using Pkg; Pkg.develop(PackageSpec(path=pwd())); Pkg.instantiate();'\njulia --project=docs --startup-file=no -e 'include(\"docs/make.jl\")'\nCommit and push the changes (after steps 4–6 succeed).\ngit add \"path/to/changed/file\"\ngit commit -m \"commit message\"\ngit push origin issue/xxx\nSubmit a pull request on GitHub.","title":"Daily Development Flow"},{"category":"section","location":"developer/#Versioning-and-Registering-(for-Maintainers)","page":"Developer Guide","text":"This project follows Semantic Versioning and the ColPrac version increment guidelines. When bumping the version, update:\n\nthe version in Project.toml\nthe version, year, and month in CITATION.bib\n\nKeep the version values synchronized, and set the citation date to the release date.\n\nTo register this package in the General registry, install Registrator and use it via the GitHub App.","title":"Versioning and Registering (for Maintainers)"},{"category":"section","location":"#AllInOne.jl","page":"Home","text":"(Image: Julia 1.12+) (Image: Colab: open) (Image: Stable) (Image: Dev) (Image: Citation) (Image: license) (Image: code style: runic) (Image: contributer's guide: ColPrac) (Image: CI) (Image: coverage) (Image: Aqua) (Image: JET)\n\nPkgFactory all-in-one template integration test","title":"AllInOne.jl"},{"category":"section","location":"#Quick-Start","page":"Home","text":"Run the following command in the Julia REPL or a notebook:\n\nimport Pkg; Pkg.add(url=\"https://github.com/ohno/AllInOne.jl.git\")\n\nAfter installation, run the following to load the package and verify it works:\n\njulia> import AllInOne; AllInOne.hello()\n\"Hello, World!\"","title":"Quick Start"},{"category":"section","location":"#User-Guide","page":"Home","text":"For detailed usage instructions and examples, see the User Guide.","title":"User Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"#Developer-Guide","page":"Home","text":"For contribution and maintenance workflows, see the Developer Guide.","title":"Developer Guide"},{"category":"section","location":"#API-Reference","page":"Home","text":"For the generated API index and docstrings, see the API Reference.","title":"API Reference"},{"category":"section","location":"#Citation","page":"Home","text":"Use CITATION.bib to cite this package.\n\n@misc{AllInOne,\n\tauthor  = {PkgFactory CI},\n\ttitle   = {AllInOne.jl},\n\turl     = {https://github.com/ohno/AllInOne.jl},\n\tversion = {v0.0.1},\n\tyear    = {2026},\n\tmonth   = {sep}\n}","title":"Citation"},{"category":"section","location":"#Acknowledgments","page":"Home","text":"This package is written in the Julia programming language, built on an initial project template generated using PkgFactory.jl. This repository is hosted on GitHub, and continuous integration is run using GitHub Actions.","title":"Acknowledgments"}]
